    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve $\\dfrac{2x-1}{x^2-3x+5}<1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x<2$ or $x>3$.\n\nThe denominator has negative discriminant and positive leading coefficient, so multiply by it directly.",
      "worked": "For the denominator,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-3)^2-4(1)(5)\\\\\\Delta&=-11<0\\end{align*}$$\n\nIts leading coefficient is positive, so $x^2-3x+5>0$ for all real $x$. Multiply both sides by this denominator.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-1&<x^2-3x+5\\\\x^2-5x+6&>0\\\\(x-2)(x-3)&>0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x<2$ or $x>3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
